        "status": {
          "description": "Whether this person is still in the world. `living` and `legend` are this block's own words for it and no other block uses the same pair -- npcs say `alive`/`dead`, villains say `living`/`fallen` -- so `liveness` beside this enum is the published translation and is what a cross-block predicate reads. Absent reads as `present`, because a record written before a package recorded departure described someone who stood. The running half of the same rule is Sim/icarus_sim/terrain_liveness.py; the two are compared by tests/test_status_vocabulary.py rather than one being derived from the other.",
